  "notes": [
    "The book divides the list into Early (1807-1809), Middle (1810-1812) and Late (1813-1814) periods. The builder doesn't enforce them: choices that belong to a period say so in their name.",
    "Up to two Cavalry Brigade regiments can be upgraded to Guard (Guard Light or Guard Heavy Cavalry).",
    "The chapter makes Light Infantry Shooting 2 (p. 56) and Guard Light Cavalry 6/-/4/3 without Elite 5+ (p. 57), and adds Guerrillas, which the list doesn't offer; the list's table (p. 110) is followed."
  ],
  "specialRules": [
    "A la Muerte: Spanish batteries that take a break test from shooting casualties only break on a 4 or less.",
    "Spanish commanders roll for aggression, independence and decisiveness (Black Powder p. 94) on 1-3 Low, 4-5 Normal, 6 High.",
    "All Spanish infantry: Must Form Square, Mixed Formation, and can form skirmish order in terrain they couldn't normally enter."
  ],
